### Error Handling Middleware
```php
class ErrorHandlerMiddleware implements MiddlewareInterface
{
    public function process(Request $request, RequestHandler $handler): Response
    {
        try {
            return $handler->handle($request);
        } catch (ValidationException $e) {
            return ApiResponse::error(
                'Validation failed',
                422,
                $e->getErrors()
            );
        } catch (NotFoundException $e) {
            return ApiResponse::error(
                'Resource not found',
                404
            );
        } catch (UnauthorizedException $e) {
            return ApiResponse::error(
                'Unauthorized',
                401
            );
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            // Log error
            error_log($e->getMessage());
            
            return ApiResponse::error(
                'Internal server error',
                500
            );
        }
    }
}
```

## API Versioning Strategy

### URL Versioning
```php
// ✅ DO: URL-based versioning
$app->group('/api/v1', function (RouteCollectorProxy $group) {
    $group->get('/questions', QuestionController::class . ':index');
    $group->get('/questions/{id}', QuestionController::class . ':show');
});

$app->group('/api/v2', function (RouteCollectorProxy $group) {
    // New version with breaking changes
    $group->get('/questions', QuestionControllerV2::class . ':index');
});
```

### Version Deprecation
```php
// ✅ DO: Signal deprecated versions
$app->group('/api/v1', function (RouteCollectorProxy $group) {
    $group->get('/questions', QuestionController::class . ':index')
        ->add(new DeprecationMiddleware('v1', '2025-12-31'));
});
```

## Best Practices

1. **Consistent Naming**: Use consistent naming conventions
2. **RESTful Principles**: Follow REST principles strictly
3. **Versioning**: Plan for API versioning from start
4. **Documentation**: Keep OpenAPI docs up to date
5. **Error Handling**: Consistent error responses
6. **Validation**: Validate all input
7. **Security**: Authentication, authorization, rate limiting

